&lt;h2&gt;


Cheat sheet
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Re-render or remount?&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Why&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Parent passes new props, same type &amp;amp; key, same slot&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Re-render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React reuses the instance; only props change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; changes on the same type at the same slot&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Remount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; overrides type/position identity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Type changes at the same slot (&lt;code&gt;isX ? &amp;lt;A/&amp;gt; : &amp;lt;B/&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Remount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Different type ⇒ React assumes a different subtree&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;{cond &amp;amp;&amp;amp; &amp;lt;Modal/&amp;gt;}&lt;/code&gt; toggling &lt;code&gt;cond&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mount ↔ unmount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The element only exists in the tree while &lt;code&gt;cond&lt;/code&gt; is true&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;List item reordered with a stable &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Re-render (instance moves with it)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Identity travels with the key, not the position&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;List item reordered with an &lt;strong&gt;index&lt;/strong&gt; key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Effectively a remount/mixup down the list&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The index, not the item, is the identity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;setState&lt;/code&gt; called inside the component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Re-render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same instance, new state, same identity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ancestor unmounts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;All descendants unmount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No slot survives without its parent&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Force a fresh instance on purpose — the documented pattern for&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// "reset this component's state when X changes":&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Chat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;conversationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;conversationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;conversationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Don't do this instead — it re-renders once with stale state,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// then a second time with the reset applied:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setDraft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;conversationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Lists: key by stable identity, never by position.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Row&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Key takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State belongs to a &lt;strong&gt;(type, key) pair at a tree position&lt;/strong&gt;, not to your component function — that's the one rule behind every re-render/remount surprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Re-render&lt;/strong&gt;: same instance, new props, existing state and effect subscriptions survive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Remount&lt;/strong&gt;: old instance torn down (cleanup runs, state discarded), new instance built from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; is your override&lt;/strong&gt; — change it to force a remount on purpose instead of syncing state in an effect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;List keys are identity, not decoration.&lt;/strong&gt; An unstable key produces exactly the "wrong item's state" bugs that a good key prevents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;StrictMode's double-invoke and the React Compiler's memoization both sit &lt;em&gt;alongside&lt;/em&gt; this rule — neither one changes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Back to that chat draft
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The draft didn't clear because &lt;code&gt;Chat&lt;/code&gt; never stopped being the same &lt;code&gt;Chat&lt;/code&gt; — React had no reason to think otherwise, because nothing about its type or its position (or, before the fix, its key) ever changed. Adding &lt;code&gt;key={conversationId}&lt;/code&gt; didn't patch around the bug; it told React the one thing it needed to know: a different conversation is a different &lt;code&gt;Chat&lt;/code&gt;, and it should be built fresh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The next time state resets when you didn't expect it — or refuses to when you did — ask the tree-slot question first: did the type or the key at that position actually change? You'll usually have the answer before you've read a single line of the component's own code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What's the state-reset bug that cost you the most time to track down — and did it turn out to be a &lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;




